+.. _JsonDataView_tasks:
+
+/-/tasks
+--------
+
+Lists every background task registered with :ref:`datasette_add_background_task`, launched or not, in registration order. For each task it shows the name, the current ``state`` (``registered``, ``running``, ``completed``, ``crashed`` or ``cancelled``), the dotted path of the ``function`` it runs, when it ``started_at``, and the ``exception`` repr if it crashed. ``launched`` reports whether the tasks have been launched yet, which distinguishes "no tasks registered" from "tasks registered but not launched yet". This endpoint requires the ``permissions-debug`` permission, since it exposes runtime internals. `Tasks example <https://latest.datasette.io/-/tasks>`_:
+
+.. code-block:: json
+
+    {
+        "ok": true,
+        "tasks": [
+            {
+                "name": "poll-for-updates",
+                "state": "running",
+                "function": "my_plugin.poll_for_updates",
+                "started_at": "2026-10-21T09:15:02.418310+00:00",
+                "exception": null
+            },
+            {
+                "name": "nightly-cleanup",
+                "state": "crashed",
+                "function": "my_plugin.Cleanup.__call__",
+                "started_at": "2026-10-21T09:15:02.419902+00:00",
+                "exception": "RuntimeError('disk full')"
+            }
+        ],
+        "launched": true
+    }
+
 .. _JsonDataView_actor:
 
 /-/actor
